      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5964e9a60248e65ef59d76be|full_name}: @{5ad7bf1b38efb048d27fc223|full_name} is correct.  I have have a total of 4 touch controllers.  2 hands and 2 \"VR Objects\".  Unity can track these VR Objects via the Oculus SDK and provides 6DOF.  Ideally the VRChat version in the Oculus store would implement this part of the SDK and treat the VR Objects like Vive trackers.  While researching this I actually discovered you can have even more than 2 VR Objects.  Each controller can be turned into an object.",
